WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:03.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We have to talk about
those boys in the cave, dude.

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, these are
the Thai boys in the cave?

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:10.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. Did you guys
talk about that at all?

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.144 line:92%
Can you believe that story?

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:13.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ask me anything
about that story.

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:13.947 line:92%
-Oh, are you fully up to date?

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:17.550
-I can't stop reading about that
story, and it keeps going.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.353
-Like, what's happening now?
-Oh, what's happening now?

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:23.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, only the boys
shaved their heads,

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:24.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they're going
into a monastery

00:00:24.591 --> 00:00:26.826 line:92%
to honor the diver that died.

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:29.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're going to go
to a monastery now.

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:31.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God.
-It's the most amazing story.

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:32.732 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-How many kids was it?

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:36.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That I don't know.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:37.037 line:92%
I don't read the fine print.

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:41.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you're not about,
like, numbers.

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:43.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're feelings.
-Yes.

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:44.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
They all got out.
-Yep.

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:47.580
-They had to -- I'm gonna
talk about this forever.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:51.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
They had to be sedated.
Did you know that?

00:00:51.518 --> 00:00:52.585 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-No. Before they went --

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:54.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, you seriously
didn't know that?

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:54.921 line:92%
Why didn't you read this story?

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:57.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was so worried it was
gonna have an unhappy ending.

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:58.291 line:92%
-I'm only talking about it

00:00:58.291 --> 00:00:59.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause it was
a happy ending, of course.

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:01.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would never talk about it
if it was a sad ending.

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:03.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, they sedated them before
they took them back?

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:04.330 line:92%
-Yes. They put them to sleep.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:08.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
They don't even remember
getting traveled in the water.

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:09.536 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Can you imagine?

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:12.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they were asleep, and
there was a diver next to them

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:16.810
just watching them to make
sure everything was going fine.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.311 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And it took hours, dude.

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:22.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was --
The tunnel was like an "S."

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:26.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, at one point,
they couldn't -- It's --

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:27.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They say that's,
of the letters,

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:30.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
the worst one
for your tunnel to be.

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:32.725 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-And -- Wait. Oh!

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:35.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the coach
that brought them there...

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:35.695 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:38.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...which, you know...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:43.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, there was an outcome
where he was not a hero, yeah.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:46.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But he had studied
to be a Buddhist monk

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:48.842
and he taught them
to meditate to conserve energy.

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:50.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they all learned
to meditate in the cave.

00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:55.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
♪♪ And they lived
off of rainwater ♪♪

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:56.249 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Why isn't every --

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:58.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I heard the coach --
I did hear that the coach

00:01:58.218 --> 00:01:59.285 line:92%
didn't eat any of his food.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:02.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. He gave away his food.
-Yeah.

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:03.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ugh!
-I mean, I guess you...

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:08.795
-I don't know why you don't talk
about this every night.

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:11.197 line:92%
Don't do any jokes about Trump.

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:14.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just talk seriously
about this story,

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.201 size:78% position:39% line:92%
'cause it never ends.

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:15.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It's amazing.

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:17.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I remember, we were --
A very similar story.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.173
We were working at "SNL"
when the Chilean miners --

00:02:20.173 --> 00:02:20.540 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh!

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.809
-That was another story that --
You loved that story.

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:24.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
-'Cause they all got out.
-Yeah.

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:26.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And remember
the Chilean miners?

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:27.981 size:78% position:39%
Ask me anything about
the Chilean miners.

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:30.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I remember
there was one Chilean miner

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:32.852 line:92%
who, like, loved the camera.

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:34.154 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Do you remember that?

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:35.788 line:92%
-He got a little popular.

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:38.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then I think
we wrote a talk-show sketch

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:40.827 line:92%
where Fred was that miner.

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:43.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then the band was,
like, the other 31 miners.

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:44.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can't remember what it was.
-Yeah.

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:46.099 size:78% position:39%
And America never saw
that sketch, right?

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:47.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. Didn't see that.
-No, no.

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:48.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think I might
have also written one where

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:53.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
there were 31 miners went in
and 32 came out.

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:57.177 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.177 --> 00:02:58.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think that's maybe
all I had, but --

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:02.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Was the 32nd miner Horatio?
-Yeah, probably.

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:02.549 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:04.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He was just a guy
who lived down there.

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:08.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
He lived in a cave and then
he saw that as his chance out.

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:09.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That should
have been on the air.

00:03:09.556 --> 00:03:11.991
-By the way, you know about what
happened to Horatio today?

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:13.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
Our friend Horatio Sanz.
-What?

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:15.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think he became
an American citizen today.

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:17.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Gasps ]
Are you kidding me?

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:18.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think that
truly happened today.

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:21.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
Give it up for Horatio Sanz.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:21.134 --> 00:03:21.901 line:92%
-America is better for it.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We'll have to
fact-check that, of course.

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:24.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We'll have to have
a party for him.

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:25.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, we have to have
an American party for him.

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:28.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that's wonderful.
-That's great news.

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:31.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, it's no Thai boys
in a cave, but it's --

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:32.145 size:84% position:42% line:92%
'Cause it's one person.

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:34.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I would say,
like, if you had to choose,

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:35.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
at a dinner party, what
to bring up,

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:37.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
either Horatio
becoming an American

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:38.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
or the Thai boys,
you would talk about --

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:41.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am not kidding when
I've just been talking nonstop

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:44.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
to people about it,
and it's been weeks now.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:45.291 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:46.759 line:92%
-It's kind of over as a story,

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:50.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it's just
beginning...for me.

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:51.130 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-You're just starting?

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:54.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They're entering
a monastery now.

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:54.834 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, no.

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:55.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
What if they get trapped
in the monastery?

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:58.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Trapped in the monastery.
They won't, they won't.

00:03:58.271 --> 00:03:59.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They won't get trapped?
-They would never.

00:03:59.706 --> 00:04:03.776
-And then the divers have to
get them out of the monastery.

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:06.279
'Cause they only -- They're only
comfortable with the divers,

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:07.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
so even though
there's no water...

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:11.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They're like,
"You're the man I trust."

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:11.618 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That would be --

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:12.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
They've got to check
those doors, make sure they --

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:16.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, 'cause I believe
most monasteries in Thailand

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:20.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
do have, like,
the hallways like an "S."

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:21.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you know --
And you know what?

00:04:21.628 --> 00:04:24.664
Elon Musk...
-Oh, great. I want to hear this.

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:26.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, Elon Musk
sent a submarine.

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:30.203 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Yeah. Period. The end.

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:31.971
You know the guy that's
always like, "I'll help,"

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:35.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's like -- And he brings
out some stupid tool

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:38.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
or something or,
like, "unclogs your sink,"

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:38.945 line:92%
by, like, taking it apart?

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:42.849
Like, I used to live above a
bunch of meth-heads in Chicago,

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:44.917
and, one time, they were like,
"We're gonna fix your sink."

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:48.655
And they just took it apart and
they left for like two weeks.

00:04:48.655 --> 00:04:51.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's what it felt like.
[ Both laugh ]

